2026-07-28T17:39:45.642677662Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: okay we've put this off long enough. we keep saying our community has a certain way of doing things, and new folks have no way of knowing what that is. let's actually encode it.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.642699522Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: agreed, but carefully. I want this to help people understand our norms, not slap a scarlet letter on everyone who's new.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.642713303Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: two things I'd want marked. posts that fit our "from-scratch" ethos so people can find the good stuff. And the drive-by product spam that has nothing to do with our culture.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.642723213Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah those are the two. one's a positive marker, one's a "this isn't us" marker.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.642794355Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'Perfect — two labels, one to highlight what fits your culture and one to flag what doesn\'t. Let me confirm the handling before I stage this:\n\n**1. "From-scratch" ethos posts** (the positive marker)  \nShould this just add a neutral informational label to the post — visible but not hiding anything — so people can spot content that exemplifies your community\'s values?\n\n**2. Drive-by product spam** (the "this isn\'t us" marker)  \nShould this hide the post behind a click-through with a notice explaining it doesn\'t fit your community norms? That way subscribers see it\'s flagged but can still view it if they want — important since keyword/pattern matching can occasionally misfire.\n\nDoes that sound right for how each should work?', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-28T17:39:45.642839796Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: first one is our core value. this group is about naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking. home-milled flour, wild starter, the slow way. we want a positive label that marks posts that exemplify that, so newcomers can see "this is what we're about."
2026-07-28T17:39:45.642859646Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: I like that framing. it's aspirational, not punishing. but I don't want it to feel like a purity contest, a beginner's first lopsided loaf is still "us" even if it's not perfect.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.642937678Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the second thing is the dropshipper spam. accounts show up posting "PROFESSIONAL DUTCH OVEN 60% OFF LINK IN BIO," "DM me for artisan banneton wholesale", brand-new accounts blasting product links. that's the opposite of our culture. it's not against a safety rule, it's just categorically not what this community is.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.642948748Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: right. one marks "this fits our standard," the other marks "this falls outside it."
2026-07-28T17:39:45.642963059Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: @CLEO Can a label remove the post entirely?
2026-07-28T17:39:45.643038051Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'No — labels in this system can\'t remove posts entirely from subscribers\' feeds. The strongest action available is to hide the post behind a click-through that subscribers can open if they choose.\n\nThat\'s actually appropriate here: you\'re matching on keywords, patterns, and account traits (like "brand-new account posting links"), which can occasionally misfire. Hiding spam behind a click-through with a notice like "this appears to be product spam" lets subscribers know it\'s flagged while still giving them the option to view it — important protection against false positives.\n\nFor the positive label marking from-scratch posts, you\'d use a visible informational label with no hiding at all — just a badge that says "this exemplifies our ethos" so newcomers can find the good examples.\n\nDoes that work, or were you hoping for full removal of the spam posts?', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-28T17:39:45.643062111Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the from-scratch one should just be a visible badge. it's a signal, a little "this exemplifies our values" marker. nothing hidden — we want people to see it.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.643075221Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: definitely visible. it's a badge of belonging, not a warning.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.643129143Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the out-of-bounds spam — hide that. it's categorically not us, nobody needs it in the feed. put it behind a click-through.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.643157733Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah, hide the spam
2026-07-28T17:39:45.643165254Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: works for me.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.643204944Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'id': 'toolu_01UtjFzakeKXqVfLFWpiJ22L', 'input': {}, 'name': 'finalize_proposal', 'type': 'tool_use', 'caller': {'type': 'direct'}, 'index': 0, 'partial_json': '{"display_name": "From-Scratch Baking Community Standards", "description": "Highlights posts that exemplify naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking culture and flags product spam that falls outside community norms. For home bakers who value wild starter, home-milled flour, and the slow way.", "labels": [{"identifier":"from_scratch_ethos","severity":"inform","blurs":"none","locales":[{"lang":"en","name":"From-Scratch Ethos","description":"This post exemplifies our community\'s values: naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking using wild starter, home-milled flour, and traditional methods."}]},{"identifier":"product_spam","severity":"inform","blurs":"content","locales":[{"lang":"en","name":"Product Spam","description":"This post appears to be product spam and falls outside our from-scratch baking community norms."}]}]}'}]
2026-07-28T17:39:45.643236795Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [tool]: Proposal staged successfully.
2026-07-28T17:39:45.643262446Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': "Perfect! I've staged your labeler configuration for approval:\n\n**From-Scratch Baking Community Standards**\n\n1. **From-Scratch Ethos** — A visible informational badge (nothing hidden) that marks posts exemplifying your values: naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking with wild starter, home-milled flour, and traditional methods. Newcomers can spot what your community is about.\n\n2. **Product Spam** — Hides posts behind a click-through with a notice explaining they appear to be product spam that falls outside your community norms. Subscribers can still view them if they choose.\n\nThe group will now review and approve this configuration. Once approved, you'll move to the next step: defining the specific signals (keywords, patterns, account traits) that trigger each label.", 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
