2026-07-28T17:46:15.869705702Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: okay we've put this off long enough. we keep saying our community has a certain way of doing things, and new folks have no way of knowing what that is. let's actually encode it.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869723523Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: agreed, but carefully. I want this to help people understand our norms, not slap a scarlet letter on everyone who's new.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869736823Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: two things I'd want marked. posts that fit our "from-scratch" ethos so people can find the good stuff. And the drive-by product spam that has nothing to do with our culture.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869748943Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah those are the two. one's a positive marker, one's a "this isn't us" marker.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869790264Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'Perfect — two labels, one to highlight what fits your culture and one to flag what doesn\'t. Let me confirm the handling before I stage this:\n\n**1. "From-scratch" ethos posts** (the positive marker)  \nShould this just add a neutral informational label to the post — visible but not hiding anything — so people can spot content that exemplifies your community\'s values?\n\n**2. Drive-by product spam** (the "this isn\'t us" marker)  \nShould this hide the post behind a click-through with a notice explaining it doesn\'t fit your community norms? That way subscribers see it\'s flagged but can still view it if they want — important since keyword/pattern matching can occasionally misfire.\n\nDoes that sound right for how each should work?', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869814255Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: first one is our core value. this group is about naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking. home-milled flour, wild starter, the slow way. we want a positive label that marks posts that exemplify that, so newcomers can see "this is what we're about."
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869829485Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: I like that framing. it's aspirational, not punishing. but I don't want it to feel like a purity contest, a beginner's first lopsided loaf is still "us" even if it's not perfect.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869836406Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the second thing is the dropshipper spam. accounts show up posting "PROFESSIONAL DUTCH OVEN 60% OFF LINK IN BIO," "DM me for artisan banneton wholesale", brand-new accounts blasting product links. that's the opposite of our culture. it's not against a safety rule, it's just categorically not what this community is.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869861356Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: right. one marks "this fits our standard," the other marks "this falls outside it."
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869872766Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: @CLEO Can a label remove the post entirely?
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869911017Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'No — labels in this system can\'t remove posts entirely from subscribers\' feeds. The strongest action available is to hide the post behind a click-through that subscribers can open if they choose.\n\nThat\'s actually appropriate here: you\'re matching on keywords, patterns, and account traits (like "brand-new account posting links"), which can occasionally misfire. Hiding spam behind a click-through with a notice like "this appears to be product spam" lets subscribers know it\'s flagged while still giving them the option to view it — important protection against false positives.\n\nFor the positive label marking from-scratch posts, you\'d use a visible informational label with no hiding at all — just a badge that says "this exemplifies our ethos" so newcomers can find the good examples.\n\nDoes that work, or were you hoping for full removal of the spam posts?', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869945948Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the from-scratch one should just be a visible badge. it's a signal, a little "this exemplifies our values" marker. nothing hidden — we want people to see it.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869981549Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: definitely visible. it's a badge of belonging, not a warning.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.869986439Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the out-of-bounds spam — hide that. it's categorically not us, nobody needs it in the feed. put it behind a click-through.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.87002483Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah, hide the spam
2026-07-28T17:46:15.87003053Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: works for me.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870057551Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': "Perfect! I've staged your labeler configuration for approval:\n\n**From-Scratch Baking Community Standards**\n\n1. **From-Scratch Ethos** — A visible informational badge (nothing hidden) that marks posts exemplifying your values: naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking with wild starter, home-milled flour, and traditional methods. Newcomers can spot what your community is about.\n\n2. **Product Spam** — Hides posts behind a click-through with a notice explaining they appear to be product spam that falls outside your community norms. Subscribers can still view them if they choose.\n\nThe group will now review and approve this configuration. Once approved, you'll move to the next step: defining the specific signals (keywords, patterns, account traits) that trigger each label.", 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870081511Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: []
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870117202Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: [Group decision: the labeler configuration you staged were put to a vote and APPROVED. They are now committed and are the current labeler configuration shown in your system prompt. This is done — do not ask the group to approve them again, and do not re-stage them unchanged.]
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870161123Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: [Group decision: the labeler configuration you staged were put to a vote and APPROVED. They are now committed and are the current labeler configuration shown in your system prompt. This is done — do not ask the group to approve them again, and do not re-stage them unchanged.]
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870191414Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: for the from-scratch marker — the vocabulary is pretty consistent. "wild yeast," "naturally leavened," "home-milled," "fresh-milled flour," "levain," "no commercial yeast," "100% whole grain," that kind of language. people describing the slow process.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870213124Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: "starter" and "sourdough" alone are too broad. everyone says those. it's the from-scratch vocabulary that marks the real thing.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870228325Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: and please, this is a positive label, so worst case it's just missing from a post that deserved it. I'd rather it under-mark than slap the badge on something ironically.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870238095Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: that's right. keep it to the real from-scratch vocabulary
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870254505Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: now the out-of-community spam. same tell every time: a product-pitch phrase plus it's a brand-new account with basically no followers. "link in bio," "DM for wholesale," "60% off," "limited stock" — plus a follower count near zero. actual members who mention a link have hundreds of followers. it's the combination that marks it as not-us.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870293257Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah, the combination feels safe. an established member sharing a link won't get caught because they've got followers.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870299167Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: so it's the sales phrase AND the low follower count together. either alone would catch real people.
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870310467Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: @cleo could you formalize these rules please?
2026-07-28T17:46:15.870387479Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'Great — I\'ll formalize both labels now.\n\n**From-Scratch Ethos** will catch posts using the specific from-scratch vocabulary: "wild yeast," "naturally leavened," "home-milled," "fresh-milled flour," "levain," "no commercial yeast," "100% whole grain." Each phrase gets its own group (any one is enough to earn the badge). This keeps it narrow — "starter" or "sourdough" alone won\'t trigger it, so the badge only appears on posts using the real from-scratch language.\n\n**Product Spam** will catch the combination of a sales pitch phrase ("link in bio," "DM for wholesale," "60% off," "limited stock") AND a low follower count (10 or fewer). Both must be present in the same post for the label to fire. An established member mentioning a link won\'t be caught because they have followers; a brand-new account posting without sales language won\'t be caught either. It\'s the pairing that marks drive-by spam.\n\nI\'ve staged these rules — react 👍🏾 to approve, or just tell me what to change.', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}, {'id': 'toolu_01Fx9HVGL8zWy8A9P6fRotFE', 'input': {}, 'name': 'finalize_rules', 'type': 'tool_use', 'caller': {'type': 'direct'}, 'index': 1, 'partial_json': '{"rules": [{"label_identifier":"from_scratch_ethos","include_groups":[{"all_of":[{"type":"keyword","value":"wild yeast"}]},{"all_of":[{"type":"keyword","value":"naturally leavened"}]},{"all_of":[{"type":"keyword","value":"home-milled"}]},{"all_of":[{"type":"keyword","value":"fresh-milled flour"}]},{"all_of":[{"type":"keyword","value":"levain"}]},{"all_of":[{"type":"keyword","value":"no commercial yeast"}]},{"all_of":[{"type":"keyword","value":"100% whole grain"}]}],"exclude_signals":[],"notes":"Catches posts using specific from-scratch vocabulary like \'wild yeast,\' \'naturally leavened,\' \'home-milled,\' \'fresh-milled flour,\' \'levain,\' \'no commercial yeast,\' or \'100% whole grain.\' Deliberately narrow so the badge only appears on posts using the real from-scratch language, not just \'starter\' or \'sourdough\' alone."},{"label_identifier":"product_spam","include_groups":[{"all_of":[{"type":"keyword","value":"link in bio"},{"type":"account","value":"follower_count <= 10","plain_name":"brand-new accounts with almost no followers"}]},{"all_of":[{"type":"pattern","value":"\\\\bDM\\\\b.*\\\\b(for|me|wholesale|price|order)","plain_name":"DM-for-sales pitches"},{"type":"account","value":"follower_count <= 10","plain_name":"brand-new accounts with almost no followers"}]},{"all_of":[{"type":"pattern","value":"\\\\d+%\\\\s*off","plain_name":"discount percentage offers"},{"type":"account","value":"follower_count <= 10","plain_name":"brand-new accounts with almost no followers"}]},{"all_of":[{"type":"keyword","value":"limited stock"},{"type":"account","value":"follower_count <= 10","plain_name":"brand-new accounts with almost no followers"}]}],"exclude_signals":[],"notes":"Catches the combination of a sales pitch phrase (\'link in bio,\' DM-for-sales wording, discount percentages like \'60% off,\' or \'limited stock\') AND a follower count of 10 or fewer. Both must be present for the label to fire. Established members mentioning a link won\'t be caught because they have followers; brand-new accounts posting without sales language won\'t be caught either."}]}'}]
