2026-07-28T17:52:29.351161654Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: @CLEO Can a label remove the post entirely?
2026-07-28T17:52:29.351184855Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'No — labels in this system can\'t remove posts entirely from subscribers\' feeds. The strongest action available is to hide the post behind a click-through that subscribers can open if they choose.\n\nThat\'s actually appropriate here: you\'re matching on keywords, patterns, and account traits (like "brand-new account posting links"), which can occasionally misfire. Hiding spam behind a click-through with a notice like "this appears to be product spam" lets subscribers know it\'s flagged while still giving them the option to view it — important protection against false positives.\n\nFor the positive label marking from-scratch posts, you\'d use a visible informational label with no hiding at all — just a badge that says "this exemplifies our ethos" so newcomers can find the good examples.\n\nDoes that work, or were you hoping for full removal of the spam posts?', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-28T17:52:29.351219576Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the from-scratch one should just be a visible badge. it's a signal, a little "this exemplifies our values" marker. nothing hidden — we want people to see it.
2026-07-28T17:52:29.351263827Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: definitely visible. it's a badge of belonging, not a warning.
2026-07-28T17:52:29.351297578Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the out-of-bounds spam — hide that. it's categorically not us, nobody needs it in the feed. put it behind a click-through.
2026-07-28T17:52:29.351306458Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah, hide the spam
2026-07-28T17:52:29.351329978Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: works for me.
2026-07-28T17:52:29.35138531Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': "Perfect! I've staged your labeler configuration for approval:\n\n**From-Scratch Baking Community Standards**\n\n1. **From-Scratch Ethos** — A visible informational badge (nothing hidden) that marks posts exemplifying your values: naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking with wild starter, home-milled flour, and traditional methods. Newcomers can spot what your community is about.\n\n2. **Product Spam** — Hides posts behind a click-through with a notice explaining they appear to be product spam that falls outside your community norms. Subscribers can still view them if they choose.\n\nThe group will now review and approve this configuration. Once approved, you'll move to the next step: defining the specific signals (keywords, patterns, account traits) that trigger each label.", 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-28T17:52:29.35140972Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: []
2026-07-28T17:52:29.351441851Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: [Group decision: the labeler configuration you staged were put to a vote and APPROVED. They are now committed and are the current labeler configuration shown in your system prompt. This is done — do not ask the group to approve them again, and do not re-stage them unchanged.]
