2026-07-28T18:07:30.807558173Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah, hide the spam
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807578743Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: works for me.
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807591974Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': "Perfect! I've staged your labeler configuration for approval:\n\n**From-Scratch Baking Community Standards**\n\n1. **From-Scratch Ethos** — A visible informational badge (nothing hidden) that marks posts exemplifying your values: naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking with wild starter, home-milled flour, and traditional methods. Newcomers can spot what your community is about.\n\n2. **Product Spam** — Hides posts behind a click-through with a notice explaining they appear to be product spam that falls outside your community norms. Subscribers can still view them if they choose.\n\nThe group will now review and approve this configuration. Once approved, you'll move to the next step: defining the specific signals (keywords, patterns, account traits) that trigger each label.", 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807614594Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: []
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807686346Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: [Group decision: the labeler configuration you staged were put to a vote and APPROVED. They are now committed and are the current labeler configuration shown in your system prompt. This is done — do not ask the group to approve them again, and do not re-stage them unchanged.]
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807705937Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: [Group decision: the labeler configuration you staged were put to a vote and APPROVED. They are now committed and are the current labeler configuration shown in your system prompt. This is done — do not ask the group to approve them again, and do not re-stage them unchanged.]
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807740927Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: for the from-scratch marker — the vocabulary is pretty consistent. "wild yeast," "naturally leavened," "home-milled," "fresh-milled flour," "levain," "no commercial yeast," "100% whole grain," that kind of language. people describing the slow process.
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807787338Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: "starter" and "sourdough" alone are too broad. everyone says those. it's the from-scratch vocabulary that marks the real thing.
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807815039Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: and please, this is a positive label, so worst case it's just missing from a post that deserved it. I'd rather it under-mark than slap the badge on something ironically.
2026-07-28T18:07:30.8078433Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: that's right. keep it to the real from-scratch vocabulary
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807896121Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: now the out-of-community spam. same tell every time: a product-pitch phrase plus it's a brand-new account with basically no followers. "link in bio," "DM for wholesale," "60% off," "limited stock" — plus a follower count near zero. actual members who mention a link have hundreds of followers. it's the combination that marks it as not-us.
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807899801Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah, the combination feels safe. an established member sharing a link won't get caught because they've got followers.
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807906731Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: so it's the sales phrase AND the low follower count together. either alone would catch real people.
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807911841Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: @cleo could you formalize these rules please?
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807963683Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: []
2026-07-28T18:07:30.807967593Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: should we keep the follower cutoff at 10?
2026-07-28T18:07:30.808014834Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: Let's do under 30
2026-07-28T18:07:30.808044794Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah let's do under 30
2026-07-28T18:07:30.808056365Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: []
2026-07-28T18:07:30.808142017Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: [Group decision: the classification rules you staged were put to a vote and APPROVED. They are now committed and are the current classification rules shown in your system prompt. This is done — do not ask the group to approve them again, and do not re-stage them unchanged.]
2026-07-28T18:07:30.808178828Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the from-scratch badges landed where I'd expect — the wild yeast and home-milled posts got marked, the plain "sourdough" ones didn't.
2026-07-28T18:07:30.808206198Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the spam label isn't showing anything though. it says the account trait isn't simulated here?
2026-07-28T18:07:30.808241959Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: so we can't see that one until it runs against real posts?
2026-07-28T18:07:30.808306491Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'That\'s right — the account signals (follower count, account age, profile picture, etc.) aren\'t simulated in the test environment, so any label that requires them won\'t fire in testing. You\'ll only see **product_spam** in action once the labeler is running live against real posts.\n\nThe good news: **from_scratch_ethos** is working exactly as you wanted — catching the real from-scratch vocabulary and leaving the generic "sourdough" posts unmarked.\n\nFor **product_spam**, the logic is solid: it requires BOTH a sales-pitch phrase ("link in bio", DM-for-sales wording, discount percentages, "limited stock") AND a follower count under 30. That combination means:\n- Established members mentioning a link won\'t be caught (they have followers)\n- Brand-new accounts posting without sales language won\'t be caught either\n- Only the combo — sales pitch from a near-zero-follower account — gets hidden\n\nYou\'ll see it start working once it\'s live and encounters those brand-new spam accounts. The from-scratch badge is already doing its job!', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
